    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` and wrote `tests/test_solution.py`; all 22 tests pass. I didn't run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates, so I can't say whether they pass.\n\nThe code is split into three small helpers, which should keep each function's complexity low. They cover subtotal and item validation, coupon validity checks, and the discount calculation. `order_total` itself applies shipping and rounds half-up to 2 places. The tests cover:\n- the shipping threshold at 100.00\n- empty orders\n- percent and fixed coupons, including the fixed-discount cap\n- expiry on the boundary date\n- used codes\n- the `min_subtotal` boundary\n- invalid kinds and values\n- bad quantities and prices\n- half-up rounding\n\nThe spec left a few points open, and I chose as follows:\n- **Check order:** coupon validity (`CouponError`) is checked before the coupon's value range (`ValueError`).\n- **Boolean quantities:** `True` and `False` are rejected as quantities.\n- **Zero-price items:** an order with items whose subtotal is 0 still pays shipping. Only a truly empty list has none.",
